{"author":{"id":"89da5fec8eff6d69dbcdd68f81be7e9163b16f34b17e978ecf3554487379f453"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1772650993,"nonce":"WKsY5U0/nq405kB5sg4RwPkraMI=","title":"Auth request stuck in approved state cannot be reset","message":"When an auth request gets into the \"approved\" state but auth-merge never executes (e.g. bad state, daemon failure), the request is permanently stuck. The API rejects all modifications:\n\n- PUT with status=pending: \"Can only modify pending or failed requests\"\n- DELETE: not_found\n- POST dismiss: \"Request is approved, cannot dismiss\"\n\nThe only workaround is creating a duplicate request, which leaves the orphan in the dashboard.\n\n**Expected**: The API should allow force-resetting or dismissing requests in any state, or at minimum allow approved→pending transitions for re-approval.\n\nMigrated from dotfiles issue e255e65.","files":null}]}